Z||000000||fiero56||06-16-2000||01:09 AM||||I have every part I need to install power locks, windows, mirrors, and trunk release, except for the power lock wiring harness that runs under the dash. Do I REALLY need this, or is it possible to just run my own wires? I have the plugs that connect to the actual lock solonoids in each door. Has anyone here installed factory power locks in a Fiero not so equipped. Where do I tap power, etc. I have window information etc from the Michigan Fiero site, but their power door lock directions are a little fuzzy to say the least. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||06-16-2000||07:16 AM||||You can make your own harness.  I am in the middle of installing pw and pdl and cruise in my 85SE.<P>The pdl gets power from the junction box near the fuse box.  This feeds a relay that is located in the quarter panel above the passenger footwell.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||06-16-2000||08:20 AM||||I'll have to go out and look at my box of parts. Glad to hear I don't have to head out and pull MORE wiring. Those dashes aren't the easiesst things to take out. I can't believe I forgot about the relay. I'll have to get it another day, damn rain.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||06-16-2000||10:42 AM||||I have installed power locks, windows, mirrors, trunk release, sunroof, rear defrost, and the sub woofer, 120. I think thats it. So if you need some help just let me know. As for the wiring I say it is easier and quicker to use the right loom with the right plugs than to make your own and splice everything in. I aM NOt saying that you cant but? Why not do it right.||||reg||1
