Z||000012||286SE'S||06-19-2000||06:47 PM||||Well, Did we answer the original question? Will the car go faster with the 120 MPH sppedometer? Just kidding.<BR>The power window and locks are part of a single harness. There is also a wire in it for the passenger side seat belt sensor that<BR>you can ignore. I think the two pieces can be separated to two pieces as their +12 and grounds are not shared. I just want to add the locks to my car. I just pulled this harness out of a car at the junkyard and Wow what a mess I left that car in. I pulled the gauges pod, radio/heater pod, center console and the whole dash board out to get to the wiring. It connects to the harnesses in each door with the big white plugs then the right side has the lock relay and ground connection for the windows. Then it goes across the back of the dash in a plastic wrapper (very nice design) and a T goes to the switches in the center console for the windows. There are two connections to the fuse box distribution block under the left speaker. The red/white (locks)is always hot, (the three orange wires, spliced together, seems to be part of the courtesy light wiring are also always hot). The orange to the windows is only on with the key in run. I tested this on the bench and was stumped untill I found that the lock relay body must be grounded and it all worked properly. I don't think I would try to recreate this harness as it is quite a  bundle and lots of the wires are heavy gauge. The lock switches wiring being hot at all times makes me want the factory stuff in my car. One thing I forgot to note was the connection on the block for the +12. Well there will be 2-5 Fieros at the yard next week for training. Thanks for letting me is tell my story.<BR>Terry<BR>Another note: On the bench those lock motors pack quite a punch Even after 15 years!<p>[This message has been edited by 286SE'S (edited 06-19-2000).]||||reg||1
